// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL3-9_FB_Intro_H_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3273865561" "Return to Mender Lazarus"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P107568523" "<color deepskyblue>Ouroboros Initiation<br><br>Part Two</color><br><br>Mender Lazarus is waiting for you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P377256966" "Well done, {HeroName}, I knew you'd pull it off! Well, I knew it because you had already pulled it off by the time we first met, but I am starting to get a headache thinking about that. <br><br>Speaking of headaches, you should probably talk to <color deepskyblue>Mender Tesseract</color> now. She can tell you about <color orange>Temporal Scaling</color>, which is why sometimes you won't be as powerful as you think you should be when you are traveling through time."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL3-9_FB_Intro_H_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P130528246" "Speak to Mender Tesseract"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3649687025" "<color deepskyblue>Ouroboros Initiation<br>Part Three</color><br><br>Go speak to <color deepskyblue>Mender Tesseract</color> and learn about <color orange>Temporal Scaling</color>. She knows the concept better than anyone. Apparently, she's a near god in her own timeline. Guess, she's not too happy about being here where Temporal Scaling so drastically affects her."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P484915548" "Great, another cave dweller sent to me by Lazarus the Luddite.<br><br>I bet he wants me to explain <color orange>Temporal Scaling</color> to you? Wonderful.  Another waste of time.  Here's an idea, experience it for yourself. <br><br>You ever hear of Outbreak? It happened a while back, your primitive scientists couldn't handle an outbreak of a plague. A bunch of your supposed 'super powered' humans handled the situation way back when.  Well someone was messing with the time-stream and started by undoing the good deed they did that day. I want you to <color orange>go back to the Outbreak incident and correct their alteration</color>. We in Ouroboros call this 'mending,' which is what we're all about here. <br><br>Well, what are you waiting for?  Get going!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL3-9_FB_Intro_H_Part5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3205218519" "Find cure for Outbreak plague"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1612682789" "<color deepskyblue>Ouroboros Initiation<br>Part Three</color><br><br>You should go and deal with what Tesseract wants, before she gets really mad."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P769257756" "You're teleported back to the time of the initial Outbreak incident in Paragon.<br><br><color orange>You feel your power drain out of you as if you were a beginning hero all over again.</color>"

